### Ledgerly API: run with Aspire (`aspire run`), then use the API's URL from the dashboard.
### Create a dev token first:  dotnet user-jwts create --project src/Ledgerly.Api --name you@ledgerly.dev
@api = https://localhost:7180
@token = paste-token-here

### List portfolios
GET {{api}}/api/portfolios
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a portfolio
POST {{api}}/api/portfolios
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Long-term ETFs", "baseCurrency": "EUR" }

### Record a trade (replace the id)
POST {{api}}/api/portfolios/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "VWCE", "type": "Buy", "quantity": 10, "price": 112.40, "tradeDate": "2026-10-01" }

### Valuation (live prices, cached, degrades gracefully)
GET {{api}}/api/portfolios/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/valuation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Import a broker CSV (202 Accepted + Location header)
POST {{api}}/api/portfolios/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/imports
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="broker.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

date,type,symbol,quantity,price,reference
2026-09-01,buy,AAPL,5,190.10,BRK-1001
2026-09-15,buy,MSFT,3,410.00,BRK-1002
--b--

### Price alert
POST {{api}}/api/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "AAPL", "targetPrice": 150, "direction": "Above" }
